{:edb/db-before-t 1803 :edb/db-after-t 1804 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535116 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:14:51.503Z" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133571 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=0$, $y=0$, and the curve $y=\\sqrt{4 - x^2}$. What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535116 false] [17592186133571 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=0,$ $y=0,$ and the curve $y=\\sqrt{4 - x^2}.$ What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133571 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/3d67d73d3ede011d6c2fe4bc9e160aa3c2af522bff6cddfcc7c351c97418e764.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt{4-x^2} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133571 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/14f102586d04e8d0746c319f2ae457a6.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt{4-x^2} \\big\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)(x + y)dA &= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}(x + y)dydx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 false] [17592186133572 1100 "If $D$ is the finite region in the first quadrant enclosed by the curves $y=3x$ and $y=x^3$, then what is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} f\\left({x,y} \\right) \\, \\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535116 false] [17592186133572 1100 "If $D$ is the finite region in the first quadrant enclosed by the curves $y=3x$ and $y=x^3,$ then what is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} f\\left( {x,y} \\right) \\, \\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133572 1145 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/f8a5fd7fc3e98d7f08b5ea48636e5de4a1a45b7a94fbe9e968789afcfe3a582c.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =3x \\\\ {x}^{3}-3x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are $0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{3}.$ Note that we disregarded the solution $x=-\\sqrt 3$ since $x\\geq 0$ in our region.\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/232f885d2230694bf62f81f5987cd2b3a12a49430d90d2cae4712c552587a48c.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq \\sqrt{3}, \\quad x^3 \\leq y \\leq 3x \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{3x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{3x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133572 1145 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/4436a12852e62e082097841fa7fa1561.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region.\n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x$:\n$x^{3}|= 3x; x^{3} - 3x|= 0; x(x^{2} - 3)|= 0$\nSo, $x$-limits are $0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{3}$. Note that we disregarded the solution $x=-\\sqrt 3$ since $x\\geq 0$ in our region.\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/f0558707f61014c153cc8376fd9a9f38.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\sqrt{3}, \\quad x^3 \\leq y \\leq 3x \\right\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)f(x, y)dA &= ∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}∫_{x^{3}}^{3x}f(x, y)dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}[∫_{x^{3}}^{3x}f(x, y)dy]dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 false] [17592186133573 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\int_0^x x^2y \\,\\textrm{d}y \\,\\textrm{d}x$." 13194139535116 false] [17592186133573 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\int_0^x x^2y \\,\\textrm{d}y \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133573 1145 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{x}x^{2}ydydx &= ∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}[∫_{0}^{x}ydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}[\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 0)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{0}^{1}x^{4}dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}∫_{0}^{1}x^{4}dx &= \\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{x^{5}}{5}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{5} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 false] [17592186133573 1145 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133574 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\:$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region below the $x$-axis enclosed by the circle $x^2 + y^2 = 4$." 13194139535116 false] [17592186133574 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\:$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region below the $x$-axis enclosed by the circle $x^2 + y^2 = 4.$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133574 1145 "Since\n\n$$\ny \\leq 0\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = 4 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad y = -\\sqrt{4-x^2}\n$$\n\nLet's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/3a70282170b649d4c76265cefd90012b.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the circle with the line $y=0$.\nSo, the $x$-limits are\n$-2 \\le x \\le 2$.\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/5833d31c6d9bf6891307c40c65594659.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region:\n\n$$\nD = \\Big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\quad -\\sqrt{4-x^2} \\leq y \\leq 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A = \\int_{-2}^2 \\int_{-\\sqrt{4-x^2}}^{0} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-2}^{2}∫_{-\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}^{0}xydydx &= ∫_{-2}^{2}x[∫_{-\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}^{0}ydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{2}x[\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{-\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}^{0}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}x(0 - (-\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}})^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}x(- (4 - x^{2}))dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}x(x^{2} - 4)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}(x^{3} - 4x)dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}(x^{3} - 4x)dx &= \\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{x^{4}}{4} - 2x^{2}]_{-2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}((4 - 8) - (4 - 8)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 0 \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 false] [17592186133574 1145 "Since $y \\leq 0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = 4\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\ny = -\\sqrt{4-x^2}.\n$$\n\nLet's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/31e7bb281a36a3676730de0883d7abd5445093713de1bbd41899cce50a7e0e48.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the circle with the line $y=0.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$-2 \\le x \\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/2a84d17b83fb1e2036c6edc0a71c5c10a58bf893c33bbf38662ebb417aab3164.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\quad -\\sqrt{4-x^2} \\leq y \\leq 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A = \\int_{-2}^2 \\int_{-\\sqrt{4-x^2}}^{0} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}x[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x(0-(-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}})^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x(-(4-{x}^{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({x}^{2}-4)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}-4x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}-4x)\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-2{x}^{2}]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((4-8)-(4-8)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186133756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331963 13194139535116 true] [17592186133756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332018 13194139535116 true] [17592186133756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332025 13194139535116 true] [17592186133757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331970 13194139535116 true] [17592186133757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332004 13194139535116 true] [17592186133757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332011 13194139535116 true] [17592186133757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332032 13194139535116 true] [17592186133757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332039 13194139535116 true] [17592186133758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331977 13194139535116 true] [17592186133758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331984 13194139535116 true] [17592186133758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331991 13194139535116 true] [17592186133758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332046 13194139535116 true] [17592186133759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332053 13194139535116 true] [17592186133759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332060 13194139535116 true] [17592186133759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332067 13194139535116 true] [17592186133759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332074 13194139535116 true] [17592186134116 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186134116 1100 "Calculate ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dA,\\,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le x}.$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186134116 1100 "Calculate $∬_(D)\\sin (x + y)dA$, where $D = {(x, y): 0 \\le x \\le \\frac{π}{2}, 0 \\le y \\le x}$." 13194139535116 false] [17592186134116 1145 "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le x}.$ \n\nSo, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]_{0}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186134117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186134117 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}^{5}\\,dy\\,dx=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186134117 1100 "What is $∫_{0}^{2π}∫_{\\sin x}^{1 + \\sin x}x^{5}dydx$?" 13194139535116 false] [17592186134117 1145 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}^{5}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}[y]_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}((1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{6}}{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32{\\pi }^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186134233 1017 #edb/ref 17592186131840 13194139535116 false] [17592186134233 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331998 13194139535116 true] [17592186134233 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535116 true] [17592186134233 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/0e05b575c22c78000a1ec235bb82cbfad3cd0cdfc6db370f19f094799b305949.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=2{x}^{2}$ and $y=1+{x}^{2},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186134233 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/q-40727.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y = 2x^{2}$ and $y = 1 + x^{2}$, as shown above, then $∬_(D)f(x, y)dA =$" 13194139535116 false] [17592186134233 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/da2895c09bc33f628626257b6d102e74875825df14ba744904e02ffa71552a02.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186134437 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186134437 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x = 1$, $x = 2$, and the curves $y = x^{2}$ and $y = 2x^{2}$. What is $∬_(D)\\frac{x}{x^{2} + y^{2}}dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535116 false] [17592186134437 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=1,$ $x=2,$ and the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=2{x}^{2}.$ What is ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535116 true] [17592186134437 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/4fec059132b7bd02cb64f864b6982c0c64a66c22646334ca199fad12097ba435.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331963 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331964 13194139535116 true] [17592186331963 1089 "q-132124" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331963 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186331963 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=4,$ $x=8,$ and the curves $y=\\sqrt{2x}$ and $y=2\\sqrt{x-4}.$ What is ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331963 1113 #uuid "e98de7f4-1849-55a0-92ab-57809365e833" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331963 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/14b4aa0c290ef70b8442c5e5176c3311f9968b7a774b52a6a2472c356f190866.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,4\\le x\\le 8,\\,2\\sqrt{x-4}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dA & ={\\int }_{4}^{8}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{\\sqrt{2x}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331965 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331966 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331967 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331968 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331969 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331968 13194139535116 true] [17592186331964 1110 #uuid "e9c6681b-daa8-537b-89af-62d3affd2790" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331965 1034 "{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{8}{\\int }_{4}^{\\sqrt{2x}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331965 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331965 1111 #uuid "e1e2601c-e30a-51df-a6de-6c3851c7679c" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331966 1034 "{\\int }_{4}^{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{8}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331966 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331966 1111 #uuid "2592a490-89bb-5c48-b3fe-80efdde843ba" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331967 1034 "{\\int }_{4}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2x}}^{2\\sqrt{x-4}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331967 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331967 1111 #uuid "9afc7218-1e33-5b2a-b9d7-f2ca32bbd05e" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331968 1034 "{\\int }_{4}^{8}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{\\sqrt{2x}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331968 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331968 1111 #uuid "faee62f5-7af3-52c2-9fcd-1e94cc3c8df5" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331969 1034 "{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\int }_{4}^{8}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331969 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331969 1111 #uuid "033d4f6a-c6f9-5b2d-9b02-972e903f6bd3" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331970 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331971 13194139535116 true] [17592186331970 1089 "q-132249" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331970 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186331970 1100 "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines $y=2x,$ $y=6-x,$ and $x=0,$ then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331970 1113 #uuid "bf1ebc54-3588-5672-a9a8-34aff8268c29" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331970 1145 "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/24d3b93e82e88bb581eff3005687ae4ee3dc3ae0d6c25fbc26f72665042ae5c6.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+6 & =2x \\\\ 3x & =6 \\\\ x & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/af61865f54494840090351296e8a1c21446787ca0b273005e7bf9c2907585adb.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,2x\\le y\\le 6-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331972 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331973 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331974 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331975 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331976 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331975 13194139535116 true] [17592186331971 1110 #uuid "6a27b813-547c-50ba-bc55-dc6da72f6616" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331972 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{6-x}{\\int }_{2x}^{2}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331972 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331972 1111 #uuid "18ca71c1-6f8e-51e3-a1e4-0e376c9d298d" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331973 1034 "{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331973 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331973 1111 #uuid "6350f6c2-9f92-5c4c-97d6-5e2448bba003" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331974 1034 "{\\int }_{2x}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331974 1111 #uuid "d631cab9-51ec-5be9-922c-27df2b638a6d" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331975 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331975 1111 #uuid "27eeec87-782e-54c7-a56b-4c01e1ed47b9" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331976 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{6-x}^{2x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331976 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331976 1111 #uuid "acd70137-e347-5c5d-95b3-df1150dbd44c" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331977 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331978 13194139535116 true] [17592186331977 1089 "q-132277" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331977 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186331977 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331977 1113 #uuid "08c24ec0-e556-5a18-b494-94cb83244cbc" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331977 1145 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[\\,y\\,]_{0}^{3x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(3x-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1)^{4}}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331979 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331980 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331981 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331982 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331983 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331983 13194139535116 true] [17592186331978 1110 #uuid "bca249b5-18bb-5137-b435-60045e37b197" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331979 1034 "3" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331979 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331979 1111 #uuid "2f58a134-f50b-5fe2-a9f0-87ecefae3db2" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331980 1034 "2" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331980 1111 #uuid "8bcdf6b2-ef20-50a1-b6f4-3eda07aa3e83" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331981 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331981 1111 #uuid "6d5d30d8-9e52-526c-928c-97a1f45d1409" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331982 1034 "1" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331982 1111 #uuid "4de1e23a-54d6-5496-b5d5-4c3bce83908e" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331983 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331983 1111 #uuid "0442ea3b-357d-53c8-b824-92b83b99af66" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331984 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331985 13194139535116 true] [17592186331984 1089 "q-132282" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331984 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535116 true] [17592186331984 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy\\,dx=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331984 1113 #uuid "a97d9c12-2933-5c3f-9e27-d7927fc2abf2" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331984 1145 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4x\\,dx & ={[2{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331986 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331987 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331988 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331989 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331990 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331986 13194139535116 true] [17592186331985 1110 #uuid "2065018f-7568-5c71-ba8f-86366d324240" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331986 1034 "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331986 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331986 1111 #uuid "1e3a7d85-670c-54ac-8adc-f2e426b9414c" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331987 1034 "2{\\pi }^{2}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331987 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331987 1111 #uuid "bd95ebcc-92f8-5f35-be91-fc86a601624b" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331988 1034 "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331988 1111 #uuid "81a72f17-9be5-5afc-bf91-23b9a4925a04" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331989 1034 "{\\pi }^{2}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331989 1111 #uuid "51c9a413-b430-5ad6-bb11-aa3c70e869e4" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331990 1034 "4{\\pi }^{2}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331990 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331990 1111 #uuid "db59b8da-eda1-5e27-8cb7-7d91f47caf59" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331991 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331992 13194139535116 true] [17592186331991 1089 "q-37859" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331991 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186331991 1100 "${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy\\,dx=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331991 1113 #uuid "890facf8-cfbe-521e-b890-2b14f7530e02" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331991 1145 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}([\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]_{1/x}^{4x})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2x}]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{1}{3}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331993 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331994 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331995 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331996 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331997 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331994 13194139535116 true] [17592186331992 1110 #uuid "089bfb55-638a-5b89-bc67-97e73646f13b" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331993 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331993 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331993 1111 #uuid "12896bde-822e-572e-8ba6-a900187844b6" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331994 1034 "\\frac{11}{6}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186331994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186331994 1111 #uuid "61faa33e-916b-5474-b93c-