[](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/a51b5dca6436e6ffd3af0d1cfa801141d97e7660e6218344011a5ac965c722c6.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=2(x-2)^{2}-1$ and $y=2-(x-2)^{2},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332018 1113 #uuid "791269bd-c71d-54eb-974f-e94bc28e8f5b" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332018 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/a15535c1eee33018c0486fd3cf1900fd151a9a23cf374c6a0ccec60ca47c64c3.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,2(x-2)^{2}-1\\le y\\le 2-(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}-1}^{2-(x-2)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}-1}^{2-(x-2)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332020 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332021 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332022 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332023 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332024 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332021 13194139535116 true] [17592186332019 1110 #uuid "3070a20d-c66c-55f1-960b-c5d09b457208" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332020 1034 "{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}-1}^{2-(x-2)^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332020 1111 #uuid "db9b5411-3bbe-5d92-abd0-ea615e62c02c" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332021 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}-1}^{2-(x-2)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332021 1111 #uuid "f359cd06-be10-5902-ac00-bac334b0ed31" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332022 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}-1}^{2+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332022 1111 #uuid "77196d11-2c7f-50ec-aa6c-fc75112add34" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332023 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}}^{(x-2)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332023 1111 #uuid "5464b05e-378e-5968-849b-45a5eeabfcc8" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332024 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{2-(x-2)^{2}}^{2(x-2)^{2}-1}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332024 1111 #uuid "21dace07-f103-5a54-9bf1-b2558e4919b7" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332025 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332026 13194139535116 true] [17592186332025 1089 "q-81329" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332025 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186332025 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=-1,$ $x=0,$ $y=4x+6,$ and the curve $y=2{x}^{2}.$ What is ${∬}_{D}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332025 1113 #uuid "4214061a-ab7b-587e-ac5a-07f10e2cd53c" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332025 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/5d56dfdb75870a251f1eb94f0305a083489ce9e8dc4b9843138cd8ef88da30ab.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 4x+6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{4x+6}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332027 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332028 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332029 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332030 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332031 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332030 13194139535116 true] [17592186332026 1110 #uuid "bc4a6fc5-395e-5567-92b7-fc6f7ebe859d" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332027 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{4x+6}^{2{x}^{2}}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332027 1111 #uuid "06b3ad92-f6e1-5413-8de5-4617cc8e7e5d" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332028 1034 "{\\int }_{4x+6}^{2{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332028 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332028 1111 #uuid "a1d022b7-4e49-51d6-8fc8-e9cf478b90a7" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332029 1034 "{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{4x+6}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332029 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332029 1111 #uuid "57b3bd96-ebe1-5590-9529-19f4d168eed0" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332030 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{4x+6}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332030 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332030 1111 #uuid "0b3b5121-869a-598f-9e25-460313108d99" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332031 1034 "{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{4x+6}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332031 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332031 1111 #uuid "e014ce7a-04b8-5a29-a85c-9f17f18a95bd" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332032 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332033 13194139535116 true] [17592186332032 1089 "q-81336" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332032 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535116 true] [17592186332032 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/c497efbb28bade962b997d7e14f5a272f0cead56f7567b1baaebae695c7c80f4.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines $y=e,$ $x=0,$ and the curve $y={e}^{x},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dA=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332032 1113 #uuid "e08c75d3-95c8-54b4-9cdf-5e4550896e07" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332032 1145 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & =e \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/95a6d9b0bc464c719311dc900967ebd06a3aa3d3004cfe5303359eecb20551e7.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{e}^{x}\\le y\\le e}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332034 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332035 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332036 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332037 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332038 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332035 13194139535116 true] [17592186332033 1110 #uuid "7e5f1ced-f2e4-5a3d-b419-5aa471935fa7" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332034 1034 "{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332034 1111 #uuid "55961f86-e2ca-5f26-86ab-0a274fd7466d" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332035 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332035 1111 #uuid "2d0075da-bb02-5284-9285-685f02ddfd6b" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332036 1034 "{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332036 1111 #uuid "53be0223-a426-59b3-b6d0-5b877713bdaa" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332037 1034 "{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332037 1111 #uuid "5a12ddb5-8fc9-53dd-95e9-4074236ed8af" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332038 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332038 1111 #uuid "5db8ef76-6ff4-5570-ad56-e6fcd7bcced6" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332039 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332040 13194139535116 true] [17592186332039 1089 "q-81340" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332039 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186332039 1100 "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=3-{x}^{2}$ and $y=x+1,$ then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332039 1113 #uuid "449fcf8c-3af3-5e89-b45f-8866876cef67" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332039 1145 "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/7316d667d7308ac5ec0f5348055d3d0e7eb90b97abaa74f5693c3151dc3b8bb1.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-{x}^{2} & =x+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+x-2 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$-2\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/aab6fb99694b518bfa9d200a75876c9e888ba1ab7d699464bc9caca360be775a.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 1,\\,x+1\\le y\\le 3-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332041 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332042 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332043 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332044 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332045 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332043 13194139535116 true] [17592186332040 1110 #uuid "3e17de0b-4ac9-5cb9-93c5-360d939e0f07" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332041 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{1}[{\\int }_{3-{x}^{2}}^{x+1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332041 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332041 1111 #uuid "a6e58716-e592-57fc-81c2-57636f3be1fe" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332042 1034 "{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332042 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332042 1111 #uuid "1eddb42c-76db-530e-913a-8cdb2bee43df" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332043 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{1}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332043 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332043 1111 #uuid "da7686a3-9aa0-5d3d-bf87-66e146de1d5a" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332044 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332044 1111 #uuid "285d8434-c927-5d41-bd36-54db2866c583" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332045 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{3-{x}^{2}}^{x+1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332045 1111 #uuid "e2f9a85e-bc44-5b4f-bf49-b007718bc397" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332046 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332047 13194139535116 true] [17592186332046 1089 "q-81353" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332046 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186332046 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy\\,dx=$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332046 1113 #uuid "edc91c22-9833-5005-b359-ebe6680861cc" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332046 1145 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{2}{3}(x+y)^{3/2}]}_{-x}^{3x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{2}{3}(x+3x)^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{3}(x-x)^{3/2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}(4x)^{3/2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx & =\\frac{16}{3}{[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}(\\frac{2}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332048 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332049 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332050 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332051 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332052 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332051 13194139535116 true] [17592186332047 1110 #uuid "0d4aff28-90e7-5490-85ed-655b1c8653ac" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332048 1034 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332048 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332048 1111 #uuid "b451b922-a443-5496-90f5-445f1fc87bad" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332049 1034 "-\\frac{16}{5}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332049 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332049 1111 #uuid "b1ee17b8-9e3c-568d-894f-6424f28d2d70" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332050 1034 "\\frac{16}{5}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332050 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332050 1111 #uuid "76fed0f5-613b-5ca3-bfd8-b4587065bca8" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332051 1034 "\\frac{32}{15}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332051 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332051 1111 #uuid "3cfeaba2-72f7-58f2-a4b7-12a2b90d54d2" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332052 1034 "-\\frac{32}{15}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332052 1111 #uuid "0f0e826d-fd6d-55bd-9980-6ae826a5bc6d" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332053 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332054 13194139535116 true] [17592186332053 1089 "q-81361" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332053 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535116 true] [17592186332053 1100 "Calculate ${∬}_{D}3x{e}^{y}\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332053 1113 #uuid "559567ed-95bb-59d3-8c41-bbeb1f57531e" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332053 1145 "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3x{e}^{y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}3x{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}3x{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{e}^{y}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x{[{e}^{y}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-{e}^{0})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x(x-1)dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{2}-3x)dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{2}-3x)dx & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =(64-24)-(1-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =40+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332055 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332056 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332057 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332058 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332059 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332059 13194139535116 true] [17592186332054 1110 #uuid "a8999b79-b7e2-5458-9e43-8a90b6381570" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332055 1034 "10" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332055 1111 #uuid "61d35717-a6a9-5f56-bb3a-fca125c6ff49" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332056 1034 "19" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332056 1111 #uuid "a2d553ac-5023-5161-9df7-5eb06345acd2" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332057 1034 "21" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332057 1111 #uuid "d31a8b62-6efd-5c2d-970b-f351d78a549e" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332058 1034 "\\frac{41}{2}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332058 1111 #uuid "30d9b519-7bd1-5c7f-bafc-d32ed8255b21" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332059 1034 "\\frac{81}{2}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332059 1111 #uuid "ba04d36b-cc64-5596-abf1-39b10004c817" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332060 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332061 13194139535116 true] [17592186332060 1089 "q-81367" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332060 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535116 true] [17592186332060 1100 "Evaluate the double integral\n${∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines\n$x=e,$ $y=e$ and the curve $y={e}^{x}.$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332060 1113 #uuid "d2d78dc5-4a32-5648-b82a-d72069352571" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332060 1145 "Let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/aa635ca5ef3198fea56d684b034de476a72e4ace2a4c51b37c6c59977036eb76.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- The line $y=e$ intercepts the curve $y={e}^{x}$ at $x=1.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$1\\le x\\le e.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/b78021a06c9fea100b75c66a619c425345cda3666d84da018895be15a53af06d.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)]}_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx & ={[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332062 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332063 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332064 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332065 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332066 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332062 13194139535116 true] [17592186332061 1110 #uuid "e76fe949-3a16-5799-9f0a-8c72c903f90d" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332062 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332062 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332062 1111 #uuid "781c76d3-5ab5-5868-a72b-33b6cc12f6ec" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332063 1034 "e" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332063 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332063 1111 #uuid "560f5905-6606-580e-9de0-d71c7203870a" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332064 1034 "\\frac{e}{2}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332064 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332064 1111 #uuid "ac6196f7-aa5c-59c8-a2ed-636910f7f23d" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332065 1034 "1" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332065 1111 #uuid "d7c92b1d-6b43-55a9-a71f-11970c5f0625" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332066 1034 "0" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332066 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332066 1111 #uuid "cf3883c4-12d8-5ea5-a315-aa689cd924af" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332067 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332068 13194139535116 true] [17592186332067 1089 "q-81774" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332067 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535116 true] [17592186332067 1100 "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}.$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332067 1113 #uuid "a3dc511f-22f2-5e83-aeb1-3756802568a4" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332067 1145 "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}x\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[y]_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{3})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{3})dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332069 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332070 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332071 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332072 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332073 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1041 "selection" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332070 13194139535116 true] [17592186332068 1110 #uuid "f42acf4b-c19b-56c6-9624-af0deeb49ad5" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332069 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332069 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332069 1111 #uuid "f2f9f392-a139-5101-aa87-79cba5753cb4" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332070 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535116 true] [17592186332070 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535116 true] [17592186332070 1111 #uuid "c97effbb-0df8-5a30-b6f1-ead0cdc253a6" 13194139535116 true] [